hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16515","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Aqram, he said: My father narrated to me that he was with his father at al-Qaa of Namirah, and a party of riders passed by us, so my father said: O my son, stay with your small cattle until I come to these people and question them, so he drew near and I drew near, and I was looking at the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was prostrating."
"16516","Waki narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Aqram al-Khuzai, from his father, he said: I was with my father Aqram at al-Qaa, he said: A party of riders passed by us and they halted at the side of the road, so my father said to me: O my son, stay with your small cattle until I come to these people and question them, he said: So he went out and I went out after him, and behold the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: So the prayer came, and I prayed with him, and I was looking at the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whenever he prostrated."
"16517","He said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Dawud, meaning Ibn Qays, narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Aqram al-Khuzai narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me that he was with his father at al-Qaa of Namirah, he said: A party of riders passed by us and they halted at the side of the road, so my father said: O my son, stay with your small cattle until I come to this party of riders and question them, he said: He drew near to them and I drew near to him, and the prayer was established, and among them was the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I prayed with them, and it is as if I am looking at the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prostrated."
